## CRITICAL: TestOptions Support

**This is the #1 forgotten step when creating new workers!**

Every new worker that supports simulated delays/failures needs corresponding fields in `TestOptionsDto`.

### Step: Add TestOptions Fields to Orchestrator DTO

**File:** `services/orchestrator/src/ingestion/dto/initiate-workflow-job.dto.ts`

For EACH new worker, add these fields to `TestOptionsDto`:

```typescript
export class TestOptionsDto {
  // For each entity, add (using workflow domain verbs):
  @IsOptional() @IsNumber() @Type(() => Number)
  validateYourEntity?: number;        // Input step processing delay (ms)

  @IsOptional() @IsNumber() @Type(() => Number)
  submitYourEntity?: number;          // Output step processing delay (ms)

  @IsOptional() @IsNumber() @Type(() => Number)
  submitYourEntityAckDelay?: number;  // ACK delay (ms)

  @IsOptional() @IsArray() @IsNumber({}, { each: true }) @Type(() => Number)
  submitYourEntityFailOnAttempts?: number[];  // Retry control

  // FOR FAN-OUT WORKERS: Add singular versions + filter field!
  @IsOptional() @IsNumber() @Type(() => Number)
  validateYourItem?: number;    // Singular for fan-out child (input step)

  @IsOptional() @IsNumber() @Type(() => Number)
  submitYourItem?: number;      // Singular for fan-out child (output step)

  @IsOptional() @IsArray() @IsString({ each: true })
  submitYourItemFailForIds?: string[];  // Failure filter for partial failure testing!
}
```

### Why This Matters

Without these DTO fields, the testOptions get **silently stripped** by class-validator during request parsing. Your test payload will include the options, but the workers will never receive them!

